**Debounced Async API Call with Cancellation Support**
=====================================================

Below is an example of a JavaScript function that debounces an async API call with cancellation support. This function utilizes a `Promise` to manage the asynchronous operation and a timeout to prevent repeated calls within a certain timeframe, allowing for cancellation of the pending operation.

```javascript
class DebouncedAPI {
  constructor(apiEndpoint, timeout = 500) {
    this.apiEndpoint = apiEndpoint;
    this.timeout = timeout;
    this.pending = null;
  }

  async call(...args) {
    // Cancel any pending request
    if (this.pending) {
      this.pending.cancel();
    }

    // Set a new pending request with a timeout
    this.pending = new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
      const timeoutId = globalThis.setTimeout(() => {
        reject(new Error("Timeout"));
      }, this.timeout);

      this.pending.resolve = resolve;
      this.pending.reject = reject;
      this.pending.cancel = () => {
        globalThis.clearTimeout(timeoutId);
        reject(new Error("Request cancelled"));
      };
    });

    try {
      // Make the API call
      const response = await fetch(this.apiEndpoint, { method: 'POST', body: JSON.stringify(args) });
      const data = await response.json();
      this.pending.resolve(data);
    } catch (error) {
      this.pending.reject(error);
    }
  }
}

// Usage example
const api = new DebouncedAPI('https://example.com/api/endpoint');

api.call({ foo: 'bar' })
  .then((data) => console.log(data))
  .catch((error) => console.error(error));

// If you want to cancel the request
api.pending.cancel();
```

**How it works:**

1.  When a new call is made, any pending request is cancelled using the `cancel` method.
2.  A new promise (`this.pending`) is created with a timeout. If the promise is not resolved within the specified `timeout`, it rejects with a "Timeout" error.
3.  When the API call is made, the response is awaited and then passed to the promise's `resolve` function. If an error occurs, the promise is rejected with the error.
4.  To cancel a pending request, call the `cancel` method on the `api.pending` promise.

